/target

# The raw NPPAD dataset is ~600MB — far too large to check into git, and it's
# already publicly hosted upstream. data/raw/ is where you fetch it into
# locally (see README "Getting the data"), but it never gets committed.
# data/results/ (EDA summaries, charts) is NOT ignored — those are small,
# checked-in, generated-but-tracked outputs, same convention as your other
# projects.
/data/raw/

# data/features/ holds the Phase 2 windowed-feature CSV (~450MB,
# 160k+ rows). It's fully deterministic from data/raw/ + core/src/features.rs
# and core/src/bin/extract_features.rs, so — same reasoning as data/raw/ —
# it's a regenerable intermediate, not something to commit. Only its small
# summary (data/results/feature_summary.json) is checked in.
/data/features/
